## Type Safety and Declarations

- Always specify types explicitly
- Declare return types on methods
- Use strict casting rules
- Avoid dynamic types completely
- Prefer final for immutable variables

```dart
// Good - explicit types
final String appName = 'Monica Companion';
List<String> getContactNames() => <String>[];
final int maxRetryAttempts = 3;

// Bad - implicit types
final appName = 'Monica Companion';
getContactNames() => [];
var maxRetryAttempts = 3;
```

## Constructor and Widget Standards

- Use const constructors everywhere
- Always include super.key parameter
- Put required parameters first
- Use trailing commas consistently
- Sort constructors before methods

```dart
// Good - const constructor with key
class WelcomeScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  const WelcomeScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Scaffold(
    body: const SafeArea(
      child: Column(
        children: <Widget>[
          // Widget content
        ],
      ),
    ),
  );
}
```

## Import Organization and Package Structure

- Use package imports only
- Sort imports alphabetically
- Group Flutter, package, relative imports
- Avoid relative lib imports
- Include package prefix correctly

```dart
// Good - package imports
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:monica_companion/core/config/app_config.dart';
import 'package:monica_companion/features/shared/models/feature_state.dart';

// Bad - relative imports
import '../../../core/config/app_config.dart';
import 'models/feature_state.dart';
```

## Code Style and Formatting

- Use single quotes for strings
- Require trailing commas on lists
- Keep lines under 80 characters
- Use expression function bodies
- Prefer null-aware operators consistently

```dart
// Good - single quotes and trailing commas
final List<String> validEmails = <String>[
  'test@example.com',
  'user@domain.org',
];

String getMessage() => 'Welcome to Monica';
String? getUserName() => user?.name;
```

## Error Handling and State Management

- Extend Equatable for state classes
- Use proper error state patterns
- Include meaningful error messages
- Override props for equality
- Handle null safety properly

```dart
// Good - proper state class @lib/features/shared/models/feature_state.dart
class ErrorState extends FeatureState {
  const ErrorState(this.message, [this.code, this.details]);

  final String message;
  final String? code;
  final dynamic details;

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => <Object?>[message, code, details];
}
```

## Documentation and Comments

- Use triple-slash doc comments
- Include meaningful class documentation
- Avoid obvious inline comments
- Document public API methods
- Follow dartdoc conventions precisely

```dart
/// Application configuration constants and settings
class AppConfig {
  AppConfig._();

  /// Application name based on environment
  static String get appName => EnvironmentConfig.appDisplayName;

  /// HTTP request timeout based on environment
  static Duration get defaultTimeout =>
      Duration(seconds: FeatureFlags.apiTimeoutSeconds);
}
```